      <title>Single-family home sells for $1.7 million in San Jose</title>
      <link>https://www.eastbaytimes.com/2026/03/06/single-family-home-sells-for-1-7-million-in-san-jose/</link>
      <description>A 1,846-square-foot single-family residence, built in 1983, has changed hands. The house in the 4400 block of George Oaks Drive in San Jose was sold on Jan. 26 for $1,715,000, or $929 per square foot. This single-story house has four bedrooms and two bathrooms. The property is equipped with a heating system. Additionally, the building includes access to two parking spots. The property is situated on a lot spanning 5,995 square feet.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.eastbaytimes.com/2026/03/06/single-family-home-sells-for-1-7-million-in-san-jose/</guid>
